---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { AUTHOR_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, SITE_NAMES } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { displayDate } from '../../lib/format';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title={`Editorial policy of ${SITE_NAMES[lang]}: sources and corrections`} description="Which legal texts and Department of Home Affairs pages AU Visa Costs relies on, which sources it refuses, how amounts are checked, and how a mistake is corrected and dated." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Editorial policy' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Editorial and corrections policy</h1>
    <p>A visa charge is paid once and is rarely refunded. A wrong total can push a family to apply without the money for the second instalment, so every amount here points to the item of the Regulations it was read in.</p>
    <h2>Who is responsible</h2><p>{AUTHOR_NAME}, reachable at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
    <h2>What we read</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>the Migration Regulations 1994 on the Federal Register of Legislation, in the latest compilation (Schedule 1 for the charges, regulations 2.12C and 2.12D for how they are made up and paid, regulation 5.37 for the employer nomination fee);</li>
      <li>the visa pages of the Department of Home Affairs, for the conditions and the length of stay, under the Department's Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 Australia licence;</li>
      <li>the Department's processing time and pricing tools, which we link to and never copy by script.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Sources we refuse</h2><p>Migration agents, law firms, education agents, forums and apps never supply an amount here, even when they publish a table: their copies date quickly and some leave out the charges for family members.</p>
    <h2>Review cycle</h2><p>Charges are read again each time a new compilation of the Regulations is registered and at least every three months, and always in the first days of July, when the yearly increase takes effect. A future amount is shown only with its start date.</p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <ol><li>We read the source again.</li><li>We correct the data file and add a test for the case.</li><li>The site rebuilds and every page shows the new date.</li></ol>
    <h2>Independence</h2><p>No government body, agent or school pays for or reviews what is published, and there is no affiliate link. See the <a href={route('method', lang)}>method page</a>. Version of <time datetime={LAST_UPDATED}>{displayDate(LAST_UPDATED, 'en-AU')}</time>.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
